# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Line-ending policy — see edge.md EC-X-01 (severity S1)
#
# Git on Windows defaults to converting LF -> CRLF in the working copy. That
# silently changes the bytes of any text the pipeline hashes or exact-matches,
# which breaks:
#   · content_hash / SimHash deduplication
#   · the 100% quote-traceability guarantee (exact substring match)
#
# A groundedness failure caused by a line-ending conversion looks identical to
# a hallucinated quote — and the tempting "fix" is to loosen the matcher, which
# destroys the guarantee outright (edge.md EC-V-10).
#
# So: force LF everywhere, and exempt the fixtures that must keep exact bytes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default: normalise to LF in the repo AND in the working copy
* text=auto eol=lf

*.md    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.toml  text eol=lf
*.cfg   text eol=lf
*.txt   text eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXEMPT: test fixtures must preserve their bytes EXACTLY.
# The CRLF/encoding fixture (edge.md §12) deliberately contains CRLF, NFD
# Unicode, mojibake and ZWJ emoji. If Git normalises it, the test that is
# supposed to catch EC-X-01 silently stops testing anything.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
tests/fixtures/**  -text
data/**            -text

# Binary
*.parquet  binary
*.gz       binary
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.pdf      binary
*.xlsx     binary
